From 6649c289995c5f6c069295311775eee2ab2edec1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MOTOR-46 (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:37:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] sync: account client fixes from the security review
 (SEGURIDAD-PORTES-23)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Review of #981 (comment 6865456375):

- K1: the first-poll baseline is only for a Mac that creates or logs in.
  A Mac that learns the account from the server (S1) always warns: the
  «cadena-ligada» bar names the email of the account and offers «No la he
  ligado yo», which leads to «Borrar la cuenta y los datos en todos».
  Events older than this Mac's own joining are skipped.
- K2: «email-cambiado» clears the stored email and polls again with the
  chain proof; changing the password, the email or the key first asks for
  the current email with the proof (it is the scrypt salt).
- O-a: a retried password change sends the same wrap, so the server
  repeats its answer.
- O-b: unanswered warnings are kept, encrypted, across restarts.
- O-c: a chain left by this Mac through Brave's own buttons, with the
  account still active, is not «cuenta borrada».
- K3 (with C1 of #977): the per-device secret is generated and kept
  encrypted; sending it waits for the wire format.

Also: warnings of a page of 100 events are no longer dropped when more
pages follow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
